\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. What shall we offer our good Lord,
\par Poor nothings, for His boundless grace?
\par Fain would we His great name record
\par And worthly set forth His praise.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Great object of our growing love,
\par To whom our more than all we owe,
\par Open the fountain from above,
\par And let it our full souls o'erflow.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. So shall our lives Thy power proclaim,
\par Thy grace for every sinner free;
\par Till all mankind shall learn Thy name,
\par Shall all stretch out their hands to Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Open a door which earth and hell
\par May strive to shut, but strive in vain;
\par Let Thy word richly in us dwell,
\par And let our gracious fruit remain.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O multiply the sower's seed!
\par And fruit we every hour shall bear,
\par Throughout the world Thy gospel spread,
\par Thy everlasting truth declare.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. We all, in perfect love renewed,
\par Shall know the greatness of Thy power,
\par Stand in the temple of our God
\par As pillars, and go out no more.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

